$X$ is normally distributed with standard deviation $9$, and $P(X<75)=0.9772$.
What is the mean?
Use $P(Z<1)=0.8413$ and $P(Z<2)=0.9772$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, x=1.1cm, y=1cm]
\fill[gray!35] (-3.6,0) -- plot[domain=-3.6:2, samples=70, smooth, variable=\x] ({\x},{2.4*exp(-\x*\x/2)}) -- (2,0) -- cycle;
\draw[thick] plot[domain=-3.6:3.6, samples=90, smooth, variable=\x] ({\x},{2.4*exp(-\x*\x/2)});
\draw[->] (-4,0) -- (4.2,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw (0,0) -- (0,-0.12) node[below, font=\small] {$\mu$};
\draw (2,0) -- (2,-0.12) node[below, font=\small] {$75$};
\node[font=\small] at (0,1.1) {$0.9772$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

$X$ is normally distributed with standard deviation $6$, and $P(X<28)=0.0228$.
What is the mean?
Use $P(Z<1)=0.8413$ and $P(Z<2)=0.9772$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, x=1.1cm, y=1cm]
\fill[gray!35] (-3.6,0) -- plot[domain=-3.6:-2, samples=50, smooth, variable=\x] ({\x},{2.4*exp(-\x*\x/2)}) -- (-2,0) -- cycle;
\draw[thick] plot[domain=-3.6:3.6, samples=90, smooth, variable=\x] ({\x},{2.4*exp(-\x*\x/2)});
\draw[->] (-4,0) -- (4.2,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw (0,0) -- (0,-0.12) node[below, font=\small] {$\mu$};
\draw (-2,0) -- (-2,-0.12) node[below, font=\small] {$28$};
\node[font=\small] at (-2.7,1.1) {$0.0228$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

$X$ is normally distributed with mean $90$, and $P(X>75)=0.9332$.
What is the standard deviation?
Use $P(Z<1.5)=0.9332$ and $P(Z<2)=0.9772$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, x=1.1cm, y=1cm]
\fill[gray!35] (-1.5,0) -- plot[domain=-1.5:3.6, samples=70, smooth, variable=\x] ({\x},{2.4*exp(-\x*\x/2)}) -- (3.6,0) -- cycle;
\draw[thick] plot[domain=-3.6:3.6, samples=90, smooth, variable=\x] ({\x},{2.4*exp(-\x*\x/2)});
\draw[->] (-4,0) -- (4.2,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw (0,0) -- (0,-0.12) node[below, font=\small] {$90$};
\draw (-1.5,0) -- (-1.5,-0.12) node[below, font=\small] {$75$};
\node[font=\small] at (1.8,1.5) {$0.9332$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
